{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The work of a stone engraver.</b> The work of a craftsman of stones. חָרַשׁ here is attached to what follows it, and therefore it has a patach at its end. And so ״חָרַשׁ עֵצִים נָטָה קָו״ (Isaiah 44) — a craftsman of wood; and so ״חָרַשׁ בַּרְזֶל מַעֲצָד״ (ibid.) — all of these are attached and punctuated." "<b>Engraving of a seal.</b> As the Targum renders: clear script, like the engraving of a signet ring — the letters gouged out within it, like the way seal rings are engraved, which are for sealing letters — script that is distinct and clear." "<b>According to the names.</b> Like בִּשְׁמֹת." "<b>Set in filigree settings.</b> The stones are enclosed in filigree settings of gold — one makes a seat for the stone in gold in the shape of a hollow fitting the measure of the stone, and sinks it into the מִשְׁבֶּצֶת. Thus the מִשְׁבֶּצֶת surrounds the stone all around, and one joins the מִשְׁבְּצוֹת to the shoulder-pieces of the ephod."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:10.840885803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}